   "title": "process-attestation 0.1: a schema-valid, signed, addressed request is not refused for an envelope reason, and any response conforms to the response schema",
   "tier": 1,
   "spec": [
    "SPEC.md:1011-1023 (7.2 consumer rules 1-13: none of the rejection grounds applies to this request, so a refusal must not carry their codes, section 8.3)",
    "SPEC.md 4.4.1 (the reply dispositions) and 7.1 item 3 (a response payload validates against the schema of its type)",
    "SPEC.md:246, :1069 (a consumer MAY require its own ext namespace and then rejects a document lacking it with malformedRequest) and SPEC.md:388 (MAY reject a non-canonical VID-typed member with malformedRequest): where the payload schema admits ext, a malformedRequest here is recorded as a note and is not escalated on the attested profile",
    "payload and response schemas of https://trusttasks.org/spec/process-attestation/0.1 (Trust Tasks specification process-attestation 0.1 (status draft) on main at bd0c05013; payload schema from the pinned @openvtc/trust-tasks 0.29.0 package)",
    "response type https://trusttasks.org/spec/process-attestation/0.1#response",
    "Mechanics only: this vector does not assert that the request is authorised or what it does (that is the deployment's governance)"
   ],
