  {
   "id": "GP-PAT-007",
   "title": "process-attestation 0.1: the payload examples the specification lists as invalid are refused (18)",
   "tier": 1,
   "spec": [
    "SPEC.md:1012 (7.2 item 2: validate the payload against the schema of the type; framework SPEC.md status draft, spec/body.md:758)",
    "SPEC.md 7.2 items 2 and 10 do not order payload validation against the authorisation decision (O-03): malformedRequest, permissionDenied and the task's own standing codes (front matter errorCodes that say the caller lacks standing) are accepted; an object lookup or state code is not, so a consumer that never validates is still caught",
    "payload.invalid-examples.json of https://trusttasks.org/spec/process-attestation/0.1: (1) Bare/unnamespaced ext key. SPEC §4.5.1 requires every immediate child of ext to be reverse-DNS namespaced. (2) Unknown top-level payload member. additionalProperties: false catches `frobnicate`. (3) Challenge below the 16-character floor. A short nonce is guessable, and anti-replay is the only integrity property the request has. (4) Digest carries base64 padding and '+'. The Artifact pattern is base64url unpadded, so a producer emitting standard base64 is rejected rather than silently compared against a differently-encoded digest. (5) Unregistered disclosure category. An enum rather than a",
    "Trust Tasks specification process-attestation 0.1 (status draft) on main at bd0c05013; payload schema from the pinned @openvtc/trust-tasks 0.29.0 package"
   ],
